      "questionType": "multiplechoice",
      "prompt": "Sipho is solving a homework problem about a wind turbine blade in the **Karoo**. The tip of the blade is positioned at the coordinate $P(-24; -7)$ in Quadrant III. Sipho argues that because $x$ and $y$ are negative, the terminal radius must be $r = -25$. Why is Sipho's argument incorrect?",
